-- Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2, batch 4: robots, the Rhino and aircraft.
-- 13 rows (printed 132-165): the X-1471 Wolfhound, X-2010 Longstrike,
-- X-2020 Rainmaker, X-2525 Faust, X-2730 Griffon, X-2750 Talon, X-4500
-- Gunman, X-4600 Sharpshooter, X-5050 Black Death and X-5001 Devastator Mk II;
-- the XM-350 Rhino; the XM-279 Earth Lifter and XM-199 Phoenix.
-- See apps/character-creator/docs/surveys/triax-2.md.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
-- EVERY NUMBER WAS READ OFF A RENDER and checked against a render again by
-- book-reconcile; no figure disagreed. Every slug was queried against
-- production vehicles and gear before this file was written.
--
-- CONVENTIONS (as the Warlords of Russia vessels):
--   cost is the lowest printed price; the full wording is in cost_note. "Not
--     available" is NULL with the wording kept.
--   Locations and weapons are in printed order; a small target carries
--     "called shot only" in its mdc_note. Hand to hand tables and sensor
--     notes are in the description.
--   A book slip (a bad metric conversion, a location printed twice, a
--     missile mix that does not add up) is stored as printed and named in
--     the row.
--   The X-5050 Black Death prints three body sections and no Main Body line;
--     mdc_main_body holds the forward section (1,000) and all three are
--     locations.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-triax-2-robots-and-aircraft.sql

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
('x-1471-wolfhound', 'X-1471 Wolfhound', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Two: a pilot and a gunner. Seating for two more, usually one or two communications officers who monitor and coordinate the 2-4 DV-39 Wolf drones attached to the robot.', 'Two (typically communications officers).', 'Running 120 mph (192 km); running does not tire the operator. Leaps 30 feet (9 m) high and 40 feet (12.1 m) across, +50% with a running start, doubled at speeds over 60 mph (96 km).', 'Not possible.', 'Walks along the bottom at one third its running speed; maximum depth one mile (1.6 km).', 'Height 11 feet (3.3 m) at the shoulder; width 9 feet (2.7 m); length 18 feet (5.4 m).', '6 tons', 350, 1, NULL, 34900000, 'Black Market 34.9 million credits; NGR Army only, not sold openly, uncommon on the Black Market.', 'German name Der Wolfhund. A wolf-shaped ground infantry assault and reconnaissance robot, Triax''s trial of animal configurations: lightly armored next to other infantry robots, but low, fast and nimble over rubble, mountains and city ruins. Its signature trick is a link to up to four DV-39 Wolf scout drones; the crew can see and hear through them or take direct control, and the pilot can draw sensor data from a drone at half the usual combat bonuses. A smoke maker in the mouth lets it appear to growl and smoke when angry, which intimidates bandits. Hand to hand uses Light Ground Robot Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.353) except the leap attack: it counts as three attacks, does 4D6+6 M.D. (doubled above 50 mph/80 km), and knocks down 15-30 foot opponents on 01-70% and anything under 12 feet on 01-90%, costing the victim initiative and two attacks. Beyond the standard NGR suite its sensors include infrared, polarization, thermo-imaging, passive night vision, telescopic optics and laser targeting; destroying the head sensors and secondary cluster strips the Robot Combat bonuses. Robot P.S. 40; two side storage compartments about 4 feet long and 1 foot deep; nuclear, 20 years. Book slips: the intro calls it the X-471 and gives the shoulder weapons a 45 degree arc, the laser cannon''s own entry says 90 degrees; the location table lists one mini-missile launcher, the weapon entry three box launchers in one housing.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.132-133'),
('x-2010-longstrike', 'X-2010 Longstrike', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Three: one pilot, one gunner/missileer and one communications officer.', 'One (or an additional copilot or gunner).', 'Running 30 mph (48 km) maximum. Leaping not possible.', 'Not possible.', 'Walks along the bottom at one third its running speed; maximum depth two miles (3.2 km).', 'Height 40 feet (12.2 m); width 28 feet (8.5 m); length 18 feet (5.5 m).', '20 tons, fully loaded', 588, 1, NULL, 29000000, 'Black Market 29 million credits; NGR Army only, not sold openly, uncommon on the Black Market.', 'German name Langenstreik. A ground artillery missile carrier, the first of the Full Militarization long-range robots (104 P.A.), built by refitting an existing industrial freight-loading robot: the cargo arms became two armored, quick-swap long-range missile pods and the roof crane a pair of gatling rail gun turrets, with Dragonwing energy arms under the chest. A spent pod can be swapped for a loaded one in under four minutes, and the pods can still take the old cargo containers or crane arms to haul wreckage or supplies. Hand to hand uses Heavy Ground Robot Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.352) with its strike and dodge bonuses halved, +1 to strike with long-range attacks, no running ram or kick, and a 3D6 M.D. stomp. Sensors add telescopic, passive night vision and polarizing optics, an advanced radar of 200 miles (320 km) that tracks 144 targets, and laser communications out to 1,000 miles (1,600 km). Its 200 M.D.C. force field regenerates fully in six hours (33 M.D.C. per hour) and is used between attacks or once the ammunition is gone. Robot P.S. 55; five storage lockers (four with an energy rifle, energy pistol, T-10 armor, water and a week of rations, one with medical supplies) plus a 50 gallon water cooler; nuclear, 20 years.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.134-136'),
('x-2020-rainmaker', 'X-2020 Rainmaker', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Four: pilot, co-pilot, a dedicated gunner and a communications officer.', 'Two.', 'Running 60 mph (96 km) maximum; climbs over rubble and rock walls unhindered on slopes up to 60 degrees. Leaping not possible.', 'Not possible.', 'Walks along the bottom of a lake or sea at one third its maximum running speed; maximum depth one mile (1.6 km).', 'Height 18 feet (5.5 m); width 13 feet (3.9 m); length 25 feet (7.6 m).', '14 tons fully loaded', 570, 1, NULL, 56000000, 'Black Market 56 million credits; NGR Army only, not sold openly, never known to have reached the Black Market.', 'Model X-2020 Regenmacher. A four-legged anti-aircraft and all-terrain assault robot whose A.I.-aided targeting tracks both low-flying Gargoyles and high aircraft, filling the sky with flak from a double-barreled turret cannon; mini-missiles and an undercarriage rail gun handle Gurgoyles and ground troops. It guards mountain regions, ruins and Gargoyle roosting grounds as well as bases, towns and borders against air raids. Hand to hand uses Heavy Vehicular Style Robots (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.352) except that it cannot punch, kick or leap kick, and its stomp does 3D6 M.D. Sensors add telescopic, passive night vision and polarizing optics and an advanced radar of 100 miles (160 km) that tracks 120 targets, plus a sensor bonus of +2 to strike with the flak cannon (not hand to hand). Its 200 M.D.C. force field regenerates in six hours (33 M.D.C. per hour) and is raised only out of combat, since the weapons cannot fire through it. Robot P.S. 45; four lockers each with an energy rifle, side-arm, T-10 armor, water and a week of rations; nuclear, 20 years.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.136-138'),
('x-2525-faust', 'X-2525 Faust', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Three: a pilot, a co-pilot and a communications officer.', NULL, 'Running 70 mph (112 km) maximum; cruising around 40 mph (64 km). Leaps 30 feet (9.1 m) high or 50 feet (15.2 m) lengthwise standing, +50% with a running start; jet-boosted leaps up to 500 feet (152 m) and rocket boosts to 1,200 feet (366 m) up.', 'Not possible (jet-boosted leaps only; thrusters also break falls).', 'Skims the surface on its belly at 100 mph (160 km/89 knots) or travels underwater at half that speed; walks along the bottom at one third its running speed. Maximum depth two miles (3.2 km).', 'Height 27 feet (8.2 m); width 15 feet (4.6 m); length 8 feet (2.4 m).', '24 tons fully loaded', 900, 1, NULL, 90000000, 'Black Market 90 million credits; NGR Army only, not sold openly.', 'A specialized melee assault robot, built in limited numbers and favored by NGR pilots who like close combat; its main job is raiding Gargoyle nests and roosts, where heavy weapons fire would be risky. Jagged buzz saw blades slide from the forearms over the hands, the fists carry an Electro-Mace style charge, and arms that fold out and rotate 360 degrees can slash at foes behind it; the head is a sensor array and the crew sits in the chest. Back thrusters give jet-boosted leaps, stop a fall in midair and let it skim water. Hand to hand uses Heavy Ground Robot Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.352) except that it can kick (6D8 M.D.) and leap kick (2D6x10 M.D.). Sensors add telescopic, passive night vision and polarizing optics; destroying the head/sensor cluster strips the Robot Combat bonuses. Robot P.S. 55; three lockers each with an energy rifle, sidearm, T-10 armor, water and a week of rations; nuclear, 20 years. The Hands line prints 130 with no ''each''.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.138-141'),
('x-2730-griffon', 'X-2730 Griffon', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Two: a pilot and a co-pilot/gunner.', NULL, 'Running 30 mph (48 km), though it hops, leaps and hovers rather than runs; running does not tire the operator. Leaps 40 feet (12.2 m) high and across from a standstill, 300 feet (91.5 m) with jet thruster-assisted leaps.', 'Hovering and flight are its natural state: maximum 300 mph (480 km) with rockets at full throttle, cruising about 80 mph (128 km); maximum altitude 10,000 feet (3,048 m), but it usually works at treetop and rooftop level.', 'Skims the surface at 100 mph (160 km/89 knots) or underwater at half that speed; walks along the bottom at one third its running speed. Maximum depth two miles (3.2 km).', 'Height 11 feet (3.3 m) in its crouching combat stance, rearing up to 20 feet (6.1 m); width 9 feet (2.7 m); length 12 feet (3.6 m).', '6 tons', 420, 1, NULL, 42500000, 'Black Market 42.5 million credits; NGR Army only, not sold openly, rare on the Black Market.', 'German name Der Griffon. An air and ground infantry assault robot built to meet Gargoyles one on one in the air, flying like a bumblebee or hummingbird from foe to foe, and able to land against Gurgoyles and enemy robots. Bipedal but hunched like a fighting rooster, it rears up to head butt with its spiked beak, rams head-first under rocket power, and fights with hooked Vibro-Blade claws, a nose ion cannon and a roll-back mini-missile launcher; its V-shaped wings fold behind the main thrusters when grounded. Losing one wing ends true flight, but thruster leaps and hovering still work. Hand to hand uses the Light Flying Robots training printed with it: +1 attack plus the pilot''s at level one and +1 at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12, the pilot''s critical strike, +3 initiative, +2 strike using energy or long-range weapons, +3 strike in melee, +2 parry, +2 dodge on the ground, +5 dodge hovering, flying or leaping, +2 disarm, +3 pull punch, +3 roll with impact. Punch, kick, head butt, elbow, beak jab and body block are as Robot P.S.; a power punch doubles damage for two attacks; a flying ram or leap kick at 100 mph (160 km) or more does double leap kick damage with an 01-80% knockdown on same-size or smaller foes (halved against twice its size), costing the victim initiative and two attacks while the robot gains initiative. Robot P.S. 40; two side compartments about 4 feet long and 1 foot deep; nuclear, 20 years. Sensors are the full optical suite: laser targeting, telescopic, passive night vision, thermal-imaging, infrared and polarization.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.141-143'),
('x-2750-talon', 'X-2750 Talon', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Two: a pilot and a co-pilot/gunner.', NULL, 'Running 50 mph (80 km) maximum. Leaps 30 feet (9.1 m) high or lengthwise standing, doubled with a running start and wings extended, up to 1,000 feet (305 m) with thruster assistance without taking flight.', 'Hover stationary, glide (silent), and up to Mach 1 or 670 mph (1,072 km); double that for high altitude dive attacks. Cruising speed 200 mph (320 km); maximum altitude 45,000 feet (13,716 m).', 'Skims the surface at 100 mph (160 km/89 knots), floats with wings fully extended, or walks along the bottom at one third its running speed. Maximum depth two miles (3.2 km).', 'Height 21 feet (6.4 m); width 9 feet (2.7 m) at the shoulders; length 7 feet (2.1 m); wingspan 36 feet (11 m) with the wings fully extended.', '20 tons fully loaded', 600, 1, NULL, 72000000, 'Black Market 72 million credits; NGR Army only, not sold openly, uncommon on the Black Market.', 'A light air infantry combat robot, built only for Triax Security Forces and the NGR military: a winged humanoid like a bigger, faster Hell Angel power armor, flying prone with Y-shaped wings separate from the arms so the hands stay free for a giant rifle, bombs or cargo. It hits less hard than the X-2700 Dragonwing but is faster and more versatile than the Griffon, used for aerial scouting and raids on mountain roosts; its rib-cage rail guns fire U-rounds that stop Gargoyles bio-regenerating for 1D6 hours, and each forearm extends a pair of sword-like Vibro-Blades. Hand to hand uses the Light Flying Robot Training printed under the X-2730 Griffon. Sensors are the full optical suite (laser targeting, telescopic, passive night vision, thermal-imaging, infrared, polarization); destroying the head strips the Robot Combat bonuses. Its 100 M.D.C. force field recovers fully in three hours, a rate of 33 M.D.C. hourly, cannot be raised while attacking, and blocks its own weapons, so it is a defensive measure for flying in and out of combat. It may also carry bombs (short-range missile damage, no strike bonus) or plant VS-101 Sonic Stun Projectors around a nest. Robot P.S. 50; a locker holding two T-25 Uber body armor suits, two rifles, a first aid kit, a week of rations, a gallon of water and personal effects; nuclear, 20 years. Book slips: the location table puts the Slammer launchers on the shoulders while the weapon entry puts them in the chest, and the intro gives the wingspan as 10.9 m against 11 m in the stat block.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.143-145'),
('x-4500-gunman', 'X-4500 Gunman', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Two: one pilot and one gunner, who works the two shoulder weapons.', NULL, 'Running 70 mph (112 km); 130 mph (208 km) when assisted by the rocket propulsion system. Leaps 15 feet (4.6 m) high or lengthwise, 25 feet (7.6 m) with a running start, 60 feet (18.3 m) rocket assisted. Full flight not possible.', NULL, 'Walks along the bottom at one third its running speed; maximum depth one mile (1.6 km).', 'Height 21 feet, 3 inches (6.5 m); width 9 feet, 7 inches (3 m); length 6 feet, 8 inches (2 m)', '12.4 to 13.2 tons depending on the load out', 610, 1, NULL, 48000000, '48 million credits on the Black Market, where it is uncommon; exclusive to the NGR Army and not sold on the open market.', 'The "Schutze" is a nimble two-crew infantry support robot of the NGR Army, fielded alone with a squad or platoon or alongside other big robots, and best at ranged fire and troop support. A laser cannon rides a track on the left shoulder, a Slammer launcher on the right (it slides behind the shoulder when idle and can be jettisoned), with rail gun arms in the rib cage, forearm pulse lasers and leg mini-missiles; either shoulder weapon can be swapped for the optional ion cannon, particle beam or grenade launcher. Hand connectors like the Ulti-Max II power a giant rifle or TX-H melee weapon from the reactor for an unlimited payload. A 100 M.D.C. force field regenerates in three hours (33 per hour) and cannot be up while it attacks or fires. Hand to hand uses Light Ground Robot Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.353) at Robot P.S. 45, plus Kicks (5D8 M.D.) and Leap Kicks (1D8x10 M.D., two attacks). Sensors add infrared, thermo-imaging, polarization, telescopic and passive nightvision optics plus laser targeting; losing the head removes all sensor bonuses. Nuclear, 20 year life; cargo locker fits personal effects, two rifles and two sets of body armor.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.145-148'),
('x-4600-sharpshooter', 'X-4600 Sharpshooter', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Two: one pilot and one communications officer.', NULL, 'Running 110 mph (176 km); 180 mph (288 km) running and jumping with the jump jets. Leaps 50 feet (15.2 m) high or lengthwise, 70 feet (21.3 m) with a running start, or 100 feet (30.5 m) high and 200 feet (61 m) lengthwise with the booster jets. Flight and hovering not possible.', NULL, 'Walks along the bottom at one third its running speed; maximum depth one mile (1.6 km).', 'Height 18 feet (5.5 m); width 8 feet, 4 inches (2.5 m); length 6 feet, 3 inches (1.9 m)', '8.5 tons', 430, 1, NULL, 42000000, '42 million credits on the Black Market, where it is uncommon; exclusive to the NGR Army and not sold on the open market.', 'The "Scharfschutzen" is a slimmer, more humanoid NGR scout and designated-sniper robot that slips behind enemy lines to call in artillery and missile strikes and pick off officers, sensor arrays and radar towers. Its main weapon is the 14 foot (4.2 m) TX-4601 Long Rifle rail cannon, whose ramjet-boosted rounds reach nearly two miles; two rocket boost jets and six directional jets let it scale towers and cliffs and clear obstacles up to 75 feet (22.9 m), and it always carries two TX-H melee weapons. Active camouflage plus heat-signature damping gives enemies -4 on Perception Rolls and -25% on Detect Concealment and Sensory Equipment rolls to find it; it also has 200 mile (320 km) radar tracking 120 targets, an infrared target painter (one mile/1.6 km, +4 to strike for the incoming strike) and laser communications to 1,000 miles (1,600 km), half in mountains or underground. A 100 M.D.C. force field regenerates in three hours and blocks its own fire. Hand to hand uses Light Ground Robot Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.353) at Robot P.S. 40, gaining +1 to dodge and +1 to disarm at first level, Leap Kicks (5D8 M.D., two attacks) and Kicks (3D8 M.D.). Cargo: a weapon locker (rifle, sidearm, light body armor, canteen, 4 weeks of rations) and a built-in water cooler printed "two gallon (38 liter)", a conversion slip for about 7.6 liters.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.148-150'),
('x-5050-black-death', 'X-5050 Black Death', 'rifts', 'robot', '12: one pilot, one co-pilot, five gunners, one artillery gunner, two communications officers, one technical officer and one unit commander.', '48-72 infantry soldiers, 8-16 flying power armor troops and 3-6 light giant robots is the standard mix; any similar combination works. Instead of troops it can haul up to 89,000 tons of cargo (as printed).', 'Running 45 mph (72 km) maximum. Leaping and flying not possible.', NULL, 'Fully amphibious: walks the sea floor at 20 mph (32 km) to a depth of 3.5 miles (5.6 km).', 'Height 30 feet (9.1 m) from toe to top of the main gun turret, with the head/forward section raised 10 feet (3 m) off the ground; width 34 feet (10.4 m); length 83 feet (25.3 m)', '102 tons fully loaded, plus troops and/or cargo', 1000, 1, NULL, 182000000, '182 million credits; NGR Army only; never sold on the open market; none seen on the Black Market.', 'A six-legged troop carrier, mobile artillery piece and miniature field base ordered when the XM-279 Earth Lifter proved too vulnerable to Gargoyle swarms; it is slow, very costly and counted among Triax''s least successful designs. Its weapons slaughter Gurgoyles, Gargoyles and Brodkil by the hundreds, but smaller, faster foes can rush it and strip its guns, so it does best inside a large combined-arms formation or guarding bases and lightly contested borders. There is no single main body: the rear, mid and forward sections are separate locations, and losing the forward or mid-section shuts it down (the forward section''s 1,000 is stored as the main body). Losing both front or both rear legs halves speed, losing the center pair cuts it 20%, and destroying both side sensor clusters removes all sensor bonuses; sensors add telescopic, passive nightvision and polarized optics plus 200 mile (320 km) radar tracking 120 targets. Hand to hand follows Heavy Vehicular Style Robots (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.352) at Robot P.S. 60, except it cannot parry, punch, kick or leap kick; a stomp does 6D6 M.D. to targets under 10 feet (3 m). Colored black and dark grey; nuclear, 20 year life. The 89,000 ton cargo figure is printed against a 102 ton machine and is stored as printed.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.150-153'),
('x-5001-devastator-mk-ii', 'X-5001 Devastator Mk II', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Eight: one pilot, one co-pilot, four gunners, one communications officer and one intelligence officer/Military Specialist; it runs at nearly full capability with half that crew.', 'Up to four additional human-sized passengers comfortably, seven in cramped conditions.', 'Running 40 mph (64 km) maximum; cruising usually 20 mph (32 km). Leaping and flying not possible.', NULL, 'Walks along the bottom at one third its running speed; maximum depth two miles (3.2 km).', 'Height 58 feet (17.7 m); width 25 feet (7.6 m) shoulder to shoulder; length 16 feet (4.8 m)', '160 tons', 2150, 1, NULL, 172000000, '172 million credits; NGR Army only; never sold on the open market; none seen on the Black Market.', '"Die Verwuestung Zwei" is the upgraded X-5000 Devastator, remaining a heavy weapons platform, now more heavily armored, with many short-range and anti-personnel systems so it can survive close assault by Gurgoyle waves; the first left the Passau line on July 6th, 108 P.A. to a nationally televised ceremony, and each mechanized unit gets two, with three each for Munich and New Berlin. A 200 M.D.C. force field takes six hours to regenerate (33 per hour) and blocks its own fire; the Shocker Field electrifies the hull against climbers but stops missile launches; losing the head removes all sensor bonuses, and sensors include all the most advanced NGR optics, sensors and radio. Hand to hand uses Elite Robot Combat Training for the pilot and co-pilot only (Heavy Ground Robot pilots get half): +1 attack plus the pilot''s at levels 2, 5, 8, 11 and 15, +2 to strike, +2 to parry, +2 to disarm, +2 to pull punch, +1 strike when using ranged weapons, no dodge or roll bonuses. Robot P.S. 60 damage: restrained punch 4D6, full punch 1D6x10, power punch 2D6x10, crush/pry/tear 1D6x10, kick 1D6x10, body flip/throw 4D6, body block/ram 1D6x10, stomp 6D6 M.D. against targets 15 feet (4.6 m) tall or smaller; no leap kick. Cargo: crew lockers, a bay with four power armor suits (typically T-31 Super Trooper, X-11 Predator II or X-535 Jaeger) and an 8x6x6 foot (2.4 x 1.8 x 1.8 m) storage bay; nuclear, 20 year life.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.153-157'),
('xm-350-rhino', 'XM-350 Rhino', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Six: one tank commander, one pilot, one co-pilot/communications officer and three laser turret gunners.', NULL, '70 mph (112 km) maximum, hovering on an air cushion two to six feet (0.6 to 1.8 m) off the ground. Cannot fly.', NULL, 'Rides on the surface at 20 mph (32 km); no underwater capability.', 'Height 10 feet (3 m); width 22 feet (6.7 m); length 40 feet (12.2 m)', '60 tons fully loaded', 800, 1, NULL, 58000000, 'Two cost lines are printed: p.157''s stat block says "Not available outside of the NGR", while p.158 lists a Black Market Cost of 58 million credits (NGR Army only, not on the open market, uncommon on the Black Market). 58 million is stored.', 'The "Nashorn" is the NGR''s new low-profile heavy hover tank, begun in answer to the Coalition''s Linebacker and built on the near-silent hover drive of the XM-330 Phantom; it is exclusive to the NGR Army and Triax Security Forces. The turret-mounted double-barrel particle beam is short-ranged for a tank gun but devastating against Gargoyle, Gurgoyle and Brodkil swarms, backed by three pulse laser turrets and a mini-missile box above the rear sensor turret. Special features: the sensor turret adds radio and laser communications to 1,000 miles (1,600 km), radar to 100 miles (160 km) tracking 120 targets, a 500 foot (152 m) motion detector and a molecular analyzer like the cyborg lung implant; the silenced drive gives an effective Prowl of 40% by day and 70% at night; the turret turns 180 degrees in one melee action; a top spotlight reaches 2,000 feet (610 m). Design bonuses: every turret gunner gains +1 attack per melee; the main gun is +1 to strike and the laser turrets +2, +1 to dodge and +5% to Pilot Tank. A 200 M.D.C. force field regenerates in six hours and is used in transit and between attacks, but the guns cannot fire while it is up; losing the rear sensor turret removes long-range communications and all sensor bonuses. The book also lists an "XM-350 Leopard III" in an NGR unit list.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.157-159'),
('xm-279-earth-lifter', 'XM-279 Earth Lifter', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Ten: one pilot, one co-pilot, three gunners, two communications engineers, two technical officers and one crew chief.', '500 infantry soldiers (no power armor or giant robots), or a common mix of 96-144 infantry, 72-96 power armor troops and 12-20 robot vehicles. Instead of troops it can carry as much as 190,000 tons of supplies and gear (as printed).', 'Not possible; lands on eight unfolding legs.', 'VTOL. Hovers stationary or moves slowly to reposition; maximum 600 mph (960 km), cruising about 300 mph (480 km); maximum altitude 40,000 feet (12,192 m).', 'Can hover above water but cannot travel on or under it; sinks like a stone.', 'Height 80 feet (24.4 m); width 90 feet (27.4 m); length 300 feet (91.5 m; the introduction gives 91.4 m)', 'Approximately 1,700 tons for the aircraft itself', 1800, 1, NULL, 380000000, '380 million credits; under a dozen in service; NGR Army only; not sold on the open market or the Black Market.', 'A 300 foot armored VTOL troop transport, the NGR counterpart to the Coalition Death''s Head Transport, that lands on any firm ground on eight legs, drops six bay doors as ramps and lifts off fully loaded in about seven seconds. It was meant to escape Gargoyle notice by not looking like an aircraft, but the enemy swarms it anyway and hunts down crashed ones, stripping them and ambushing recovery teams, so it mostly flies inside the NGR, Poland and other areas Gargoyles do not hold, usually escorted by flying power armor, robots or aircraft. A 400 M.D.C. force field (12 hours to regenerate) is raised in transit, on landing and takeoff and while idle; weapons cannot fire and troops cannot disembark while it is up, and it fails if the rear Force Field Generators section is depleted. Its own sensors add a 2,000 foot (610 m) thermal imager, infrared and ultraviolet optics, and enhanced radar tracking 192 targets to 200 miles (320 km); it is +2 to dodge at cruising speed and +3 above 300 mph (480 km), and trained NGR pilots get +10% to fly it. Like every NGR aircraft it carries the standard systems of p.159-160 on top of the usual Triax robot and vehicle features: a combat and targeting computer (+1 to strike), secure high-bandwidth links to 32 aircraft within 200 miles (320 km), a Hindsight rear radar (30 miles/48 km, 60 degree cone), an I.F.F. transponder (225 miles/360 km), imaging radar and tracking computer (200 miles/320 km in a 180 degree forward arc, 144 targets, terrain following), an inertial navigation computer (+20% Navigation), a laser communications array (about 10 miles/16 km, double on very clear days), laser targeting (10 miles/16 km, +5 to strike for laser-guided munitions), a magnetic anomaly detector (one mile/1.6 km radius from 6,000 feet, one mile underwater or 10 feet/3 m underground, double range for electromagnetic devices), a radar detector, and an anti-missile radar/radio jammer (15 miles/24 km, 01-45% success, up to two dozen frequencies). Storage holds crew weapons and T-25 armor, 20 first aid kits with RMK and IRMSS kits, and two weeks of food and water; nuclear, 20 year life. The 190,000 ton cargo figure and a 100 foot target given as 27.4 m are printed slips.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.161-163'),
('xm-199-phoenix', 'XM-199 Phoenix', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Five: one pilot, one co-pilot, one communications officer and two gunners.', '22 Jaeger-sized units, 16 Ulti-Max II or Gunman-sized units, or 44 human troops/parachuters; or up to 22 cargo (deployment) pods in 22 transport slots with 44 carrying clamps.', 'Driving on ground 10 mph (16 km).', 'VTOL. 670 mph (1,072 km) maximum; cruising 300 mph (480 km); maximum altitude 50,000 feet (15,240 m); flying range effectively unlimited.', NULL, 'Height 22 feet (6.7 m); width/wingspan 55 feet (16.8 m), folding to 30 feet (9.1 m) wide for storage; length 100 feet (30.5 m)', '30 tons unloaded', 400, 1, NULL, 34000000, '34 million credits; NGR Army only; not sold on the open market or the Black Market.', 'A bigger, heavier VTOL relative of the XM-180 Dragonfly, with three carrying pylons instead of one, used as a combat supply and troop drop ship (the stat block calls it a Mobile Fortification Transport): it usually stays at high altitude and drops power armor, robots and deployment pods rather than landing in enemy territory, and it can be hidden in warehouses or under tarps instead of on an airfield. Hated by the Gargoyles like every aircraft, about one third of those sent into combat never return. Losing one wing or the tail halves its speed and altitude without a crash, but both wings or a wing and the tail bring it down; destroying both sensor domes removes all sensor bonuses. A 200 M.D.C. force field regenerates in six hours and is used in transit, on landing and takeoff and while idle; weapons cannot fire and troops cannot leave while it is up. Like every NGR aircraft it carries the standard systems of p.159-160 on top of the usual Triax robot and vehicle features: a combat and targeting computer (+1 to strike), secure high-bandwidth links to 32 aircraft within 200 miles (320 km), a Hindsight rear radar (30 miles/48 km, 60 degree cone), an I.F.F. transponder (225 miles/360 km), imaging radar and tracking computer (200 miles/320 km in a 180 degree forward arc, 144 targets, terrain following), an inertial navigation computer (+20% Navigation), a laser communications array (about 10 miles/16 km, double on very clear days), laser targeting (10 miles/16 km, +5 to strike for laser-guided munitions), a magnetic anomaly detector (one mile/1.6 km radius from 6,000 feet, one mile underwater or 10 feet/3 m underground, double range for electromagnetic devices), a radar detector, and an anti-missile radar/radio jammer (15 miles/24 km, 01-45% success, up to two dozen frequencies). Crew storage holds a rifle, sidearm and light body armor each; nuclear, 20 year life.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.163-165');

